    "_about":  "Per-room atmosphere for the true-colour renderer. Classes apply in order to every room their list names (\u0027*\u0027 = all rooms), later classes overriding earlier ones; then rooms\\\u003cROOM\u003e.json on top. Colours are #RRGGBB. Lights: x y z in the room\u0027s own coordinates, dir = which way it faces (gives it shadows), power 1 = as bright as painted at the light, range = distance at which it is down to half, flicker 0..1. Dust: color = in the flashlight beam (adds light); colorDark + darkAlpha = the grey-brown specks seen with the flashlight off. GRAPHICS CARD ONLY: mist = fog lying on the floor under the player (density per unit at the floor, height = units over which it thins away, max, color, wisps 0..1 = how patchy, wispSize = units across a wisp, drift = units a second); embers rise from every flickering light (rate a second per light, rise, life, size, color; rate 0 = none); drips fall from the ceilings near the player (rate a second, radius, size, color); steam rises from the floor near the player (rate, radius, rise, life, size, alpha, color); kickup = dust at the feet while walking (puffs per step, step = units a step, size, life, alpha, color).",
